    "result_text": "All tests green. `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are a base class and helper; `AcceptanceTest` (3 tests) is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, region-validated `postcode` field for owners.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `postcode` column with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `postcode` (string) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, the field flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response DTO (`OwnerDto`); MapStruct maps it by name automatically, and the openapi-generator regenerates both DTOs at build time.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `validatePostcode(postcode, city)`, called during `addOwner`:\n   - `null` postcode \u2192 accepted (optional, backward-compatible).\n   - Must be exactly 4 digits, else 400.\n   - Region resolved from a fixed city table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD). If the city has no known region, any 4-digit postcode is accepted.\n   - Otherwise the value must fall within the region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else 400.\n   - 400s are raised via the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`, which the advice already maps to `BAD_REQUEST`.\n\n4. **DDL** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column to the `owners` table. The test profile (`hsqldb`, `ddl-auto=none`) relies on `schema.sql`, so this was required.\n\n**One bug caught during testing:** `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE rather than returning null, so an unknown city crashed the valid-postcode path. I fixed it by resolving the region first and returning early when it's null.\n\nThe stored/returned value is preserved verbatim (e.g. `\"2000\"`), matching the spec.",
